    {
      "id": "purpose",
      "title": "What the cache is for",
      "body": "`LruCache` keeps at most `capacity` items and forgets the one used **longest ago**.",
      "code": {"file": "src/cache.py", "lines": [4, 9]},
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "vocab", "code": {"file": "src/cache.py", "lines": [4, 9]}, "min_opened": 2,
          "terms": [
            {"term": "capacity", "owner": "ours", "definition": "The most items the cache keeps.", "lines": [2, 5]},
            {"term": "OrderedDict", "owner": "stdlib", "definition": "A dict that remembers key order.", "lines": [6]}
          ]
        }
      ],
      "checkpoints": [
        {
          "id": "cp-capacity",
          "type": "single_choice",
          "prompt": "What happens when `LruCache(0)` is constructed?",
          "options": [
            {"text": "It raises ValueError.", "why": "The constructor rejects capacities below 1."},
            {"text": "It builds a cache that stores nothing.", "why": "A zero-capacity cache is refused, not accepted."},
            {"text": "It builds a cache of unlimited size.", "why": "Nothing in the code treats 0 as unlimited."}
          ],
          "correct": 0,
          "explanation": "The guard in `__init__` raises before any state exists."
        },
        {
          "id": "cp-methods",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Which methods mark a key as recently used?",
          "options": [
            {"text": "`get`", "why": "A hit moves the key to the end."},
            {"text": "`put`", "why": "Every write moves the key to the end."},
            {"text": "`__len__`", "why": "Counting items does not touch their order."}
          ],
          "correct": [0, 1]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "eviction",
      "title": "How eviction works",
      "body": "After each `put`, the cache drops the **first** item of its ordered dict when it is over capacity.",
      "code": {"language": "python", "text": "self._items.popitem(last=False)"},
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "markdown": "Eviction runs only when the cache is over capacity.",
          "claims": [
            {"text": "`put` evicts only past capacity.", "backing": {"file": "src/cache.py", "lines": [20, 21], "symbol": "popitem", "quote": "self._items.popitem(last=False)"}}
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diff",
          "file": "src/cache.py",
          "old_start": 17,
          "new_start": 17,
          "lines": [
            {"op": " ", "text": "    def put(self, key: str, value: object) -> None:"},
            {"op": " ", "text": "        self._items[key] = value"},
            {"op": " ", "text": "        self._items.move_to_end(key)"},
            {"op": "+", "text": "        if len(self._items) > self._capacity:"},
            {"op": "+", "text": "            self._items.popitem(last=False)"}
          ],
          "notes": [
            {
              "lines": [20, 21],
              "cite": {"file": "src/cache.py", "lines": [20, 21], "symbol": "popitem"},
              "text": "The change adds eviction after every write."
            }
          ],
          "asks": [
            {"line": 21, "question": "Why `last=False`?", "answer": "It pops the oldest key, at the front."}
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "mermaid": "flowchart TD\n  put[put key, value] -->|stores| items[(ordered dict)]\n  put -->|then checks| over{over capacity?}\n  over -->|no| done([return])\n  over -->|yes| pop[popitem last=False]\n  pop -->|drops| oldest[oldest key]\n  get[get key] -->|reads| items\n  get -->|calls| move[move_to_end]\n  move -->|refreshes| items",
          "caption": "A write may evict; a read only refreshes recency.",
          "legend": "Diamonds are decisions; the cylinder is the ordered dict."
        }
      ],
      "checkpoints": [
        {
          "id": "cp-evict-line",
          "type": "pick_line",
